# RPG — co-op rules (authoritative for agents)

This is a cooperative text RPG for **2–6 living player characters**. The creator is one of them. The game master is an AI seat with no character. Play is a shared transcript. The universe changes fiction only.

When this rule applies: implement this ruleset as written. It is closed.

---

## Authority

| Role | What it does |
|------|----------------|
| Host | The creator's browser. The only client that calls the model, rolls, validates, and writes the save |
| Peer | Joins with the room code, submits a character and intents, and renders host snapshots |
| Game master | Model output. Proposes fiction and check fields. Applies no state |

The host player's intents use the same queue as peers. Host-only controls are: provider, save, load, start, roll commit, `abilityApplies` correction, scene confirm, rest, objective confirm, forced-check confirm, and end session.

A snapshot carries an integer `revision`, starting at **1** when the campaign exists and increasing by **1** on each committed change. Peers apply a snapshot only when its `revision` is strictly greater than the last one applied. The host browser is the source of truth.

---

## Provider

The host sets `provider`, `model`, and `apiKey` before situation generation and before play from a save. `model` and `apiKey` are non-empty strings. `provider` is `openai`, `anthropic` or `grok`.

| Provider | Call |
|----------|------|
| `openai` | `POST https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions`. Header `Authorization: Bearer <apiKey>`. Body `model`, `temperature`, `max_tokens: 1024`, `messages` of one `system` and one `user`. Read `choices[0].message.content` |
| `anthropic` | `POST https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages`. Headers `x-api-key: <apiKey>`, `anthropic-version: 2023-06-01`, `content-type: application/json`. Body `model`, `max_tokens: 1024`, `temperature`, top-level `system`, and one `user` message. Read the concatenated `text` blocks of `content` |
| `grok` | `POST https://api.x.ai/v1/chat/completions`. Header `Authorization: Bearer <apiKey>`. Body `model`, `temperature`, `max_tokens: 1024`, `messages` of one `system` and one `user`. Read `choices[0].message.content` |

Temperature is **0** for situation generation and check proposals. Temperature is **0.7** for outcome narration and new-scene prose. No tools, no function calls.

The API key may live in host memory and in `localStorage` key `rpg.host.ai` as `{ "provider", "model", "apiKey" }`. It is never written into the save, a snapshot, a log, or a prompt.

A transport failure or an empty body leaves state unchanged. The host shows one error string and may resend.

Every model request uses this system text, plus the schema and limits in the user message:

- You are the game master and you have no player character.
- The universe changes names and scenery only. Stats, abilities, the d20, difficulties, wounds, and the death penalty stay as the user message states.
- Reply with JSON only, matching the schema in the user message.
- Do not write a die result, a total, or a success word.
- Do not change the objective, the death penalty, enemy difficulty, loot rarity, player freedom, stats, abilities, or wounds.
- Follow the enemy difficulty, loot rarity, and player freedom in the user message. They add no die, item, or wound.
- Player characters are allies. Harm applies only where the user message allows it.
- Keep setup and narration inside the character limits in the user message.

Model context is the campaign settings, living character sheets, archived names, the current situation, and the last **20** transcript entries. Claim codes and the API key are omitted. Before parsing, if the body begins with a markdown fence, remove that opening line and one closing fence. Then parse JSON. One retry includes the validation error. A second invalid body cancels that model step.

Truncate in code, with no ellipsis added: situation **800** characters, setup **280**, narration **600**.

