## Campaign

Settings are required for a new campaign and immutable after generation. The host collects them in three steps: universe (`campaignName`, `universe`, and when `universe` is `custom` also `universeLabel` and `universeType`), team (`playerCount`, `deathPenalty`), and game (`objective`, `enemyDifficulty`, `lootRarity`, `playerFreedom`). Every field on the current step is required before the next step.

| Field | Rule |
|-------|------|
| `campaignName` | Trimmed, 1–60 characters, no CR or LF |
| `universe` | `star-wars`, `dungeons-and-dragons`, `alien`, or `custom` |
| `universeLabel` | `null`, or 1–40 trimmed characters when `universe` is `custom`. Display labels for the presets are Star Wars, Dungeons & Dragons, and Alien |
| `universeType` | `fantasy`, `science-fiction`, `horror`, `modern`, `historical`, or `post-apocalyptic`. The host chooses it only when `universe` is `custom`. A preset sets it from the table below |
| `playerCount` | Integer 2–6, including the host. The game master is told this count. It does not change the 2–6 living-character limits |
| `objective` | Trimmed, 1–280 characters, no CR or LF |
| `objectiveStatus` | Starts `active`. Later `complete` or `failed` |
| `deathPenalty` | `wounded`, `out-of-scene`, or `new-character` |
| `enemyDifficulty` | `easy`, `standard`, `hard`, or `severe`. The game master prefers check difficulty 8, 10, 12, or 15 in that order. Another legal difficulty is still allowed when the fiction requires it |
| `lootRarity` | `scarce`, `uncommon`, `common`, or `abundant`. How often useful gear appears in the fiction. There is no inventory and no loot roll |
| `playerFreedom` | `narrow`, `guided`, or `open`. `narrow` permits only actions inside the current situation. `guided` permits any action the scene can contain. `open` permits any action the character could attempt. The host still accepts a well-formed intent. The attempt can still fail |

Choosing `star-wars`, `dungeons-and-dragons`, or `alien` writes that row onto `universeType`, `playerCount`, `deathPenalty`, `enemyDifficulty`, `lootRarity`, and `playerFreedom`, replacing any previous values. `custom` clears those fields and does not fill them. `campaignName`, `universeLabel`, and `objective` are never filled or cleared by a universe change. The host may edit a filled value before generation.

| Universe | `universeType` | `playerCount` | `deathPenalty` | `enemyDifficulty` | `lootRarity` | `playerFreedom` |
|----------|----------------|---------------|----------------|-------------------|--------------|-----------------|
| `star-wars` | `science-fiction` | 4 | `wounded` | `standard` | `uncommon` | `open` |
| `dungeons-and-dragons` | `fantasy` | 4 | `new-character` | `standard` | `common` | `guided` |
| `alien` | `horror` | 3 | `new-character` | `severe` | `scarce` | `narrow` |

The host requests `{ "situation": string }` at temperature 0. An empty situation after trim is invalid. If both attempts fail, the host stays on settings and no campaign is stored. Scene **1** is that situation. The host then creates their character and the lobby opens.

