## Save `schemaVersion: 1`

Every commit also writes the save JSON to `localStorage` key `rpg.host.save`. If that write throws, play continues and the host shows one error. Download name: slug of `campaignName` plus `.rpg.json`. The slug is trimmed, lowercased, spaces turned into `-`, characters outside `[a-z0-9-]` removed, repeated hyphens collapsed, and end hyphens removed. An empty slug becomes `campaign`.

Load is a file pick or the current `rpg.host.save`. The host sets the provider again after a load. Validation failure rejects the whole document with one reason. There is no partial load.

A document is valid only when every rule here holds. Otherwise the host rejects it with one reason. `schemaVersion` is `1`. Enums and string limits match this rule. Stats are a permutation of `2`, `1`, and `0`. Wounds are a legal prefix. Names are unique ignoring case. Non-archived count is **0–6**. `lobby` has **1–6** non-archived characters and none archived. `play` or `ended` has **2–6** non-archived characters when none are archived, and **0–6** when at least one is archived. At most one character is non-archived with `owner: "host"`. A non-archived character with `inScene: false` has wounds `[]` or a `down` box. `roomStatus` is session-only, starts `open`, and is absent from the save.

```json
{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "campaignName": "Ashreach",
  "universe": "star-wars",
  "universeLabel": null,
  "universeType": "science-fiction",
  "playerCount": 4,
  "objective": "Recover the beacon before the storm hits.",
  "objectiveStatus": "active",
  "deathPenalty": "wounded",
  "enemyDifficulty": "standard",
  "lootRarity": "uncommon",
  "playerFreedom": "open",
  "scene": 1,
  "situation": "The party stands at the beacon's outer door.",
  "revision": 1,
  "phase": "lobby",
  "forcedCheckCharacterIds": [],
  "openCheck": null,
  "intentQueue": [],
  "characters": [
    {
      "id": "pc_00000000",
      "name": "Ada",
      "abilityId": "fighter",
      "stats": { "might": 2, "finesse": 1, "wits": 0 },
      "wounds": [],
      "claimCode": "ABCD",
      "owner": "host",
      "archived": false,
      "inScene": true
    }
  ],
  "transcript": []
}
```

`openCheck` is null or `{ "id", "kind", "actorId", "targetId", "stat", "difficulty", "failure", "abilityApplies", "assist", "setup", "committed", "line" }`. `kind` is `act`, `treat`, or `force`. On `act`, `targetId` is null and wounds apply to `actorId`. On `treat`, wounds apply to nobody and healing applies to `targetId`. On `force`, `actorId` is null and wounds apply to `targetId`. `id` is `chk_` plus 8 lowercase hex digits. `assist` is null or `{ "allyId", "status": "pending" | "accepted" | "declined" }`. `intentQueue` holds accepted intents that are not yet the open check. After load, `revision` continues; the next commit adds 1. A new room code is issued. A non-risky `act` never opens a check: the host appends the intent and the setup as narration in that commit.

Transcript entries are append-only and use these `type` values: `situation` (`scene`, `text`), `intent` (`characterId`, `kind`, `text`), `check` (`characterId`, `line`), `narration` (`text`), `wound` (`characterId`, `wounds`), `death` (`characterId`, `penalty`), `scene` (`scene`), `objective` (`status`), `system` (`text`).

---

## Systems in this game

The game is this list: three stats, eight abilities, one d20, difficulties 8 / 10 / 12 / 15, three wound boxes, three death penalties, one assist, host rolls, host model calls, a 6-character room code, and save schema version 1. Enemy difficulty, loot rarity, and player freedom are instructions to the game master. An implementation adds no other resolution, character, or session system.
